WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our next guest
has a new stand-up special,

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.167
"Look At You,"
streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:08.033
Please welcome the very funny
Taylor Tomlinson.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:16.567
♪♪

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.701
-Thank you so much!

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.968
Oh, my God.
It's so good to be here.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.834
It has been
a rough couple of years.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.667
I got bangs at one point.
Things got dark.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.334
I didn't want bangs.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.167
I just needed people
to check on me, and --

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.868
It works, by the way.
You post a selfie in bangs,

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:36.100
everybody's like, "Fire emoji.
You go, girl!"

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.234
Then they text you, like,
"You okay?"

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.300
Here's what I did.
I got bangs,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.000
and then two days later, I did
mushrooms for the first time.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.534
And as soon
as I did those mushrooms,

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:52.968
I was like, "I should've
done these first."

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.067
Probably wouldn't have gotten
these bangs

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.267
if I forgave myself, huh?

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.667
But you know what?

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:03.133
Having bangs feels exactly like
being on mushrooms.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.767
The whole time, you're just
looking at your friends like,

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:07.100
"Do I look weird?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.234
"You guys would tell me
if I looked weird, right?"

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.200
They're like, "Don't tell her.
She'll freak out."

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.767
I finally
found an anti-depressant

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.701
that works for me,
which is great.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.000
A lot of my friends
scared me by getting on them.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.067
I had a lot of friends
who were like,

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.167
"I tried to get
on anti-depressants.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.701
I just didn't like
how I felt on them.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.767
I didn't
feel like myself on them."

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.067
And now that I'm on them,
I'm like "Yeah, me neither.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.501
It's the best!"

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:33.367
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.634
Right?

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.567
And I do feel like myself.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.501
I just feel like
now someone's sitting on me,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.501
going, "Shh!
Stop talking.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.934
We are trying to help you.
You will ruin everything.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:48.334
Go to sleep.
Choose a different adventure."

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:51.934
I didn't know anti-depressants

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.400
were an option
when I was growing up.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.567
When I was in high school,
I was like,

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:55.801
"Dad, I think I'm depressed,"

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.400
and he was like,
"You just need some protein.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.300
Get a scoop of peanut butter."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.267
Yeah, there's a lot of
conservative dads out there

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:05.033
just white-knuckling it
through life right now,

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:09.067
clinging to a jar of chunky Jif
like it's the answer.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:12.434
Just a buoy in the storm.
Like, "It'll pass!"

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:16.634
The only mental-health advice
my dad ever gave me is,

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.100
I was having panic attacks
in high school,

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.467
and I didn't know
what they were, and I was like,

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.767
"I don't know what to do
when I feel like this.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.067
I don't know what to do.
I don't know what to do."

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.868
And he goes, "All right.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:29.601
All I can tell you is that
when you feel like this,

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:33.968
get as far away from the people
you care about as possible."

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:38.267
"Until you feel different."

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.334
Which is advice
you give a werewolf.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:44.033
Like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:49.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:53.267
"Just run into the woods till
you're not a monster anymore.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.601
Don't let them see you change.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:59.133
They won't accept you
for what you truly are."

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.634
I did read something recently
that said

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.200
if you had
a difficult childhood,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.667
you need to learn how to parent
yourself as an adult.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:06.667
So I've been trying to do that.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:07.968
I've been trying
to parent myself.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.634
But I kind of feel like
I got pregnant with me

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:13.534
in high school and, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:17.100
...I was not ready
for this responsibility.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.100
Not supposed to shake me.
Just found that out.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:24.033
And now every day,
I wake up totally overwhelmed.

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:25.901
Just like, "Okay.

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:29.467
If I let you watch TikTok
on my phone for 40 minutes,

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.501
will you please stop crying?"

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:39.534
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:40.901
All my friends are like,
"Are you okay?"

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.367
I'm like,
"No, I think I have colic.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.501
I kept me up all night."

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:45.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.200
Lot of my friends
are settling down.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.467
Some of them are just settling,
end of sentence.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.701
You guys have those couples
in your lives?

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.000
Yeah.
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.300
Yeah, where one person
in the couple is way hotter

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.300
and cooler than the other person
in the couple?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.934
I like to call those couples
chocolate-covered raisins.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.534
'Cause they're like, "Sure, you
could put those two together...

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:09.634
If you want."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:10.968
But every time you see them,
you're like,

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:13.534
"Chocolate, what are you doing?
Like...

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:14.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:15.834
Like, you could've been
with anybody.

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:16.868
You could've been with caramel,

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:17.901
you could've been with
marshmallow,

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:18.934
you could've
been with peanut butter,

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.334
who I heard cures depression..."

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:28.167
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.968
"...and you want to be
with a raisin forever?

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.667
Like, no offense, raisin.
You're great.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.434
We love you.
Nature's candy -- that's you.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:38.033
But you belong
with, like, oatmeal.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:39.501
Like, let's be honest."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.934
Aren't you scared every day
that someone's gonna come along

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:45.067
and suck chocolate
right off of you?

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.801
I love doing that joke
because I like to feel

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.467
couples in the audience
getting nervous.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.000
Like,
"Am I chocolate or raisin?"

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.033
"We're both chocolate,
right, babe?

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.434
We're chocolate-covered
chocolate?

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.901
We're like the little Lindor
guys in the foil, you know?

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:01.434
I'm the creamy part,
and you're the shell

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.334
'cause you're so strong and if
you leave me, I'll be a mess?"

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:05.734
Thank you so much,
"Tonight Show."

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.267
I appreciate it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.300
♪♪

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.234
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:13.334
Didn't see the peanut-butter
callback coming at all!

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:15.567
Taylor Tomlinson!

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.000
That is how you do it
right there.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.968
"Look At You"
is streaming now on Netflix.

